BMP_C Folder contains files for the bmp module operated by the Raspberry Pi Pico. 

BMP.c is our main file for the folder. Before the pico will start up the BMP sensor and initilize at an altitude that was not reflecting the relative altitude probably 
due to noise start up. So I changed up the how the altitude was calculated and added a FOR loop to filter out the startup noise when powering up. Now the altitude sits
at a 0 with a margin of error within the decimals.

Disclaimer: I am writing this long after i finished the software. But I remember the numbers drifting slightly up after a while of it running. 
I have not gone back to figure out why that happens. 
